,"warn.gave_up_loop":"{loop} leads back to itself, so it never ends. Give one of them a value that does not lead back.","warn.gave_up_deep":"Each value brings in another, more than {passes} deep. Check whether a variable refers to itself, or shorten the chain.","warn.or_target_unset":"The value is empty, and or: falls back to {target}, which nothing gives a value to. Set {target}, or write {text} to use it as text.","warn.refused":"decluttering-card-plus: left {which} in the card rather than substituting. {why}","warn.refused_transform":"A transform only shapes text, so it needs a scalar value - applying one to a mapping or a list would garble its JSON. Give the variable a scalar value, or drop the transform.","warn.refused_resolver":"A resolver reads its value as an entity id and asks Home Assistant, so it needs one that exists and carries what was asked for.","warn.refused_condition":"An if: step keeps a value only while its condition holds. Add ? to drop the option when it does not, or a default: to show something in its place.","warn.refused_json":"json turns the variable's own value into JSON text, so it has to come first in the chain. There is no step that turns text back into a mapping or a list.","warn.refused_raw":"raw gives the variable's value as it was written, before anything else is done to it, so it has to come first in the chain.","warn.refused_yaml":"yaml turns the variable's own value into YAML text, so it has to come first in the chain. There is no step that turns text back into a mapping or a list.","warn.unresolved":"decluttering-card-plus: {whose} uses {which}, which nothing gives a value to, so it is rendered as written. Set it on the card, or give it a default in the template. To write those brackets on purpose, escape it as [[{escape}]].","warn.no_item_template":"decluttering-card-plus: {whose} uses {which}, but there is no item template called {names} here, so it is rendered as written. Check the name, that the template has an item: body rather than card:, and that it is in this dashboard's decluttering_templates.","warn.unresolved_template":'template "{name}"',"warn.unresolved_this":"this template","warn.unresolved_item_in":'item template "{item}" in template "{name}"',"warn.unresolved_item":'item template "{item}"',"warn.translation_missing":"decluttering-card-plus: {whose} looks up {keys}, which none of its languages has a text for, so it is rendered as written. Add it to the template's language: block.","warn.nothing_for":'nothing in Home Assistant for "{value}"',"warn.no_map_match":'"{value}" matches none of the map: pairs',"warn.refused_map":"map: only gives a value for the pairs it names. Add *=something to catch every other value.","warn.no_pick_match":'no entry has {field} = "{value}"',"warn.pick_written":"pick: is written field=value, with the field to give after a comma if you want one, such as pick:name=dog,icon","warn.pick_not_list":'pick: looks through a list or a mapping, and "{value}" is neither',"warn.pick_not_list_after":'pick: has no list to look through after {step}, which gave "{value}". Write pick: straight after the name, or after a step that gives a list, such as to_list',"warn.refused_pick":"pick: gives nothing when no entry has that value, or the entry it finds has no such field. Add |default:something after it.","warn.unknown_step":"decluttering-card-plus: {which} The placeholder is left in the card as written.","warn.unknown_step_one":'{placeholder}: "{step}" is not a step this card knows.',"warn.step_not_alone":"{step} can only be followed by if:, unless:, flat, entries or registry","warn.with_not_alone":"with: can only be followed by if: or unless:","warn.registry_no_keys":"{arg} has none of a registry source's keys (area, domain, entities, label and so on), so |registry finds nothing in it. Use |entries to go through its entries.","warn.fills_itself":"{name} fills itself in without end","warn.read_too_deep":"decluttering-card-plus: {names} is built from other values more than {depth} deep, so it was used part-built. Shorten the chain of values it is made from.","warn.too_many_fills":"more than {max} copies would be filled in across this card, so the rest are left","warn.not_a_list_source":"{arg} is not a list, a mapping or a registry source","warn.flat_after_repeat":"flat only works straight after a repeat:","warn.not_a_mapping":"{arg} is not a mapping","warn.condition_closed":"its if: or unless: condition does not hold","warn.json_not_first":"json can only be the first step","warn.raw_not_first":"raw can only be the first step","warn.yaml_not_first":"yaml can only be the first step","warn.kind_list":"a list","warn.kind_mapping":"a mapping","warn.override_misplaced":'decluttering-card-plus: this card\'s {key}: block is ignored - the template "{template}" builds a {kind}, so only a {kind}: block is laid over it.',"warn.tag_taken":"decluttering-card-plus: <{tag}> is already registered by something else, skipping it.","trace.built":"decluttering-card-plus: {label} built in {ms} ms","trace.inside":"(inside {chain})","trace.inside_at":"(inside {chain}, at {path})","trace.copy":"Copy {number} of {count}","trace.variables":"Variables, and where each came from:","trace.placeholders":"Placeholders, and what each became:","trace.none":"(none)","trace.item":"Item template {placeholder}","trace.item_values":"Its values, as each ended up:","trace.removed":"Taken out:","trace.result":"Built:","trace.in_full":"decluttering-card-plus: {label} in full, with the cards inside it built","trace.never_built":"Never built, so left as written (hidden, not shown yet, or in error):","trace.col_variable":"variable","trace.col_value":"value","trace.col_from":"from","trace.col_placeholder":"placeholder","trace.col_became":"became","trace.col_final":"worked out to","trace.col_how":"how","trace.a_list":"(a list)","trace.a_mapping":"(a mapping)","trace.worked_empty":"(nothing)","trace.from_let":"let:","trace.from_card":"this card","trace.from_repeat":"the repeat"